# One Class Per File

- Put **at most one** top-level class, Cubit, UseCase, Repository, Model, Entity, or Widget per `.dart` file.
- Do **not** add a second class, mixin, or enum into an existing file — create a new file instead.
- File name must match the type (`app_button.dart` → `AppButton`, `login_cubit.dart` → `LoginCubit`).
- Private helpers (`_Foo`) that belong only to that type may stay in the same file; extract if reused elsewhere.

## Allowed exceptions

- Freezed / generated parts (`part` / `part of`) remain as generated by the tool.
- A Cubit and its states may stay together **only** if the project already does that for that feature; prefer separate files when adding new Cubits.
---

# Example

```dart
// ❌ BAD — two widgets in one file
class Header extends StatelessWidget { ... }
class Footer extends StatelessWidget { ... }

// ✅ GOOD — one file each
// header.dart → class Header
// footer.dart → class Footer
```
